# CVE-2024-23342: python-ecdsa Minerva attack vulnerability
# Status: Accepted with justification
# Details: This vulnerability is a side-channel attack on ECDSA signing that requires:
#   1. Access to precise timing information across multiple operations
#   2. Ability to send many requests to extract timing data
#   3. Sophisticated cryptanalytic capabilities
# 
# Our threat model does not include timing side-channel attacks. ECDSA is used only for
# JWT signing/verification in a server environment via python-jose[cryptography]. The
# cryptography library's native implementation is preferred when available, and timing
# attacks are not a practical concern for our use case.
#
# Action: Monitor for ecdsa v0.19.2+ release and upgrade immediately.
# Reported: 2026-03-17
# Next Review: 2026-06-17

CVE-2024-23342
